
KBO PySpark Machine Setup Requirements
====================================

Use this checklist on EVERY Windows machine that will execute the KBO PySpark code.

1. JAVA
--------
Install:
- Java JDK 17 (Eclipse Temurin 17)

Verify in CMD:
    java -version
    javac -version

Expected:
- Java 17.x.x


2. PYTHON
---------
Install:
- Python 3.11+ (Python 3.11 is recommended for this setup)

Verify:
    python --version


3. PYTHON LIBRARIES
-------------------
Open CMD and run:

    python -m pip install pyspark xlsxwriter jupyter

Required packages:
- pyspark
- xlsxwriter
- jupyter

Verify:

    python -c "import pyspark; print(pyspark.__version__)"
    python -c "import xlsxwriter; print(xlsxwriter.__version__)"

Working versions from our setup:
- PySpark 4.2.0
- XlsxWriter 3.2.9


4. WINDOWS HADOOP FILES
-----------------------
The Windows machine also needs:

    C:\hadoop\bin\winutils.exe
    C:\hadoop\bin\hadoop.dll

Verify:

    C:\hadoop\bin\winutils.exe

It should display the winutils usage/help.

Set HADOOP_HOME:

    setx HADOOP_HOME C:\hadoop

Add Hadoop to PATH:

    setx PATH "%PATH%;C:\hadoop\bin"

IMPORTANT:
After using setx, CLOSE CMD and open a NEW CMD window.

Verify:

    echo %HADOOP_HOME%

Expected:

    C:\hadoop


5. SPARK TEST
-------------
After Java, PySpark, and Hadoop are installed, test Spark with:

    python -c "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession; spark=SparkSession.builder.master('local[*]').appName('test').getOrCreate(); print('SPARK OK:', spark.version); spark.stop()"

Expected:

    SPARK OK: 4.2.0

Some Spark WARNING messages are normal.


6. JUPYTER
----------
Start Jupyter with:

    jupyter notebook

Then open the notebook and run the KBO Python/PySpark code there.


7. KBO DATA
-----------
For the QUICK MASTER code, the input folder must contain:

    enterprise.csv
    denomination.csv
    address.csv
    contact.csv

Example:

    C:\Users\Lenovo\Desktop\KBO_DATA

Set INPUT_FOLDER in the code to that folder.


8. OUTPUT
---------
The code creates Excel files in OUTPUT_FOLDER.

Example:

    C:\Users\Lenovo\Desktop\KBO_QUICK_RESULT

Make sure the disk has enough free space for the generated XLSX files
and Spark temporary files.


9. IMPORTANT
------------
Do NOT install pandas specifically for the KBO processing code.
The current KBO code uses PySpark + XlsxWriter.

Do NOT run the old giant full-join/repartition version if the disk is
short on space. The current quick version avoids repartition() before
Excel export.


QUICK INSTALL COMMAND
=====================
After Java is installed, run:

    python -m pip install pyspark xlsxwriter jupyter


